    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** Your frontend bundle is too large. How do you reduce it?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use code splitting, tree shaking, dynamic imports, and analyze with bundle tools. Remove unused dependencies and compress assets."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Route-based code splitting with React.lazy",
          "Component-level splitting for heavy UI (charts, editors)",
          "Analyze with source-map-explorer or webpack-bundle-analyzer",
          "Replace large libraries with lighter alternatives",
          "Enable gzip or Brotli compression on the server"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "language": "tsx",
        "code": "const Dashboard = lazy(() => import('./Dashboard'));\n\nfunction App() {\n  return (\n    <Suspense fallback={<Loading />}>\n      <Dashboard />\n    </Suspense>\n  );\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
